{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790098413,"nonce":"fVuP1t7PjLNyrVe3kBXTb9/EaS8=","message":"Revised 2026-09-22 (f4bac00), superseding the comment above; doc/design/config-entity.md is rewritten. One entity PER configurable thing — field, type, relation, flow, view, rule — under refs/config/\u003cid\u003e, kind fixed in the create op; no singleton, no flat path map. Six generic ops: Create{kind,key}, SetAttr{name,value}, RemoveAttr, SetItem{id,value} (enum values, allowed parents), RemoveItem, SetArchived (soft removal; refs cannot be deleted across clones). Structural op.Validate frozen; semantic rules in cache.ConfigCache.Update(fn), computed inside the write lock (E6). Built-ins title/type/status/archived are code (schema.Builtins); a field entity with a built-in key overrides its configurable parts (values, name, on_open/on_close) and cannot change kind or be archived (E4); no entities at all = built-ins alone. Duplicate (kind,key): lowest create lamport then id wins, loser reported and archivable (E7). Fields carry on: issue|iteration and role from a closed set (E3). RepoCache.Schema() compiles built-ins plus all unarchived field/type/relation entities, memoised by ref hashes (E8). Import validates the whole document then writes one entity at a time; N entities = N commits (E9). Commands: schema [init|export|import|log|rm] (E10). Package: entities/config (Item), schema/, cache/config_*.go, commands/schema.","files":null}]}